From a64ae8d5a2318ab0698f2b2f30c5ef4213f0a409 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: will <wrouesnel@wrouesnel.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:23:18 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Support remote clients taking over local seat sessions

- handover: in a local seat session, wait for a handover object to appear
  instead of giving up when none exists yet; disconnect the remote client
  (ERRINFO_LOGOFF_BY_USER) when the session becomes active on its seat again;
  refuse clients while it is active; hold a logind sleep/idle inhibitor while a
  client is attached; never log a local session out when the system daemon
  goes away.
- system: follow RemoteId changes on displays whose initial remote id was
  unknown and restart the handover for them.
- system: fix a double unref of the RedirectClient signal parameters.
- session-rdp: add GRD_SESSION_RDP_ERROR_LOGOFF_BY_USER.
---
